# EMove class-table row, move-REASSIGN shape (#37 Phase 2): `w = !v` to an
# EXISTING local — this is the shape that defeats a per-position move-bind
# hook (the family is keyed by the SOURCE name `v`, but the later mutation
# goes through `w`), which is why the EMove class is covered by the
# cow_moved_names ELIGIBILITY EXCLUSION rather than hooks: the `s` bind
# falls back to the eager clone and prints the PRE-mutation value.
#
# ⚠ MOVE-SHAPE ORACLE EXCEPTION: Rust gg Phase 1 is VALUE-WRONG on this
# shape (the HIGH Rust TODO) — asserted through the SELF-HOST route,
# EXPECTED-WRONG in runtime_diff, NO snapshot until the Rust fix lands.
void main():
    Vector[String] v = ["hello", "world"]
    Vector[String] w = ["seed"]
    String s = v.get(0).unwrap()
    w = !v
    w.set(0, "mutated")
    print(f"s = {s}")
    print(f"w0 = {w.get(0).unwrap()}")
